# Event registration

Registration page. On signup: the registrant gets a confirmation email, the
organizers get an alert with reply-to set to the registrant.

## Deploy in five minutes

1. **Get an App Password.** Google Account -> Security -> 2-Step Verification
   (turn on) -> App Passwords. Copy the 16 characters. Your normal Gmail
   password will not work for SMTP.
2. **Push this repo to GitHub.**
3. **Import it at vercel.com/new.**
4. **Settings -> Environment Variables.** Add every line from `.env.example`,
   with real values. `ORGANIZER_EMAILS` is the one people forget.
5. **Deploy, then register yourself on the live URL** before sending the link
   to anyone else.

## Edit your details

- `api/register.js` - the `EVENT` block at the very top
- `public/index.html` - the visible copy, and the `CONFIG` object at the bottom

## Test locally

    cp .env.example .env     # then fill it in
    npm install
    npm run dev              # http://localhost:3000

## Keep a spreadsheet of registrations

Set `REGISTRATIONS_WEBHOOK_URL` and every signup gets POSTed there as JSON.
For a Google Sheet: add headers `registeredAt, name, email, cohort,
organization, role, notes`, then Extensions -> Apps Script:

    function doPost(e) {
      const d = JSON.parse(e.postData.contents);
      SpreadsheetApp.getActiveSheet().appendRow([
        d.registeredAt, d.name, d.email, d.cohort, d.organization, d.role, d.notes
      ]);
      return ContentService.createTextOutput("ok");
    }

Deploy -> New deployment -> Web app -> execute as *me*, access *Anyone*.
Paste the URL into the env var.

## If email isn't arriving

| Symptom | Cause |
|---|---|
| `Invalid login` | Using an account password instead of an App Password / API key |
| `Missing environment variables` | Not set in the Vercel dashboard |
| Works locally, fails deployed | Env vars not added to the host |
| Lands in spam | `MAIL_FROM_EMAIL` domain has no SPF/DKIM. Send from the same domain as the SMTP account |
